    "result_text": "Green build. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`riskFlag` is a read-only boolean on the owner response, true when **any** of the three risk signals holds, false otherwise. I reused the existing signals rather than re-deriving them:\n\n| Signal | Source (reused) |\n|---|---|\n| Possible duplicate | `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` \u2014 already computed by `AssignPossibleDuplicate` and stored on the owner |\n| Email domain disposable-adjacent | new `DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(...)` |\n| City over soft capacity | new `CityCapacity.overSoftCapacity(...)` |\n\n### Files touched\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean, `readOnly`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets it.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", ignore = true)`, matching how `capacityWarning`/`bulkSignupWarning` (also repository-dependent) are handled.\n- **`CityCapacity`** \u2014 added `overSoftCapacity` = `count >= WARNING_THRESHOLD` (the soft-capacity threshold, 40). Unlike the existing `warningRaised` (40\u201349 only), this stays true for a full city too, so an at-limit city still flags.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomains`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent`: keyed off the same blocklist, true when the domain is a subdomain of a blocked domain (`inbox.mailinator.com`) or shares a blocked domain's base label under a different suffix (`mailinator.net`). Exact blocklist matches return false here since they're already rejected outright by `RejectDisposableEmail` (400), so they never reach a created owner.\n- **`OwnerRisk`** (new) \u2014 a small policy class composing the three signals; single responsibility, no logic of its own.\n- **`OwnerResponses`** (new) \u2014 collapses the three-line \"map + stamp derived flags\" block that was duplicated across `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, and `RespondWithOwnerUpdated` into one helper, and adds `riskFlag` there so all three single-owner responders stay consistent.\n\n### Design notes\n- `riskFlag` is computed at response time (not stored) because the city-capacity component depends on the other owners \u2014 same reasoning already applied to `capacityWarning`.\n- The list responders (`ListOwners`, `ListOwnersPage`) don't set these derived flags today; I kept that convention rather than expanding scope.\n\nThe visible test (`riskFlag` false for a normal owner) passes, and the full suite is green.",
